# Files git should ignore.
#
# Anything listed here stays on your PC and is never recorded in the project
# history. Two reasons something lands in this list: it is GENERATED (so there
# is no point saving it), or it contains REAL data - hostnames, staff names,
# ticket exports - that should not be copied around.

# --- Generated output --------------------------------------------------------
# Action logs, remote-session transcripts, audit reports. Created as you use the
# toolkit. Contains real machine names and staff names, so it stays local.
/output/
Jira Scripts/output/

# Local data written by the toolkit itself - e.g. data\UsersOU-Paths.json (a dump
# of the live AD structure) and "Jira Scripts\data\org-dept-map.json" (built from
# real ticket history: real site/org names). This is REAL organisation data and
# must never be committed. Regenerate the AD dump with:
#   scripts\maintenance\Get-UsersOUPaths.ps1
/data/
Jira Scripts/data/

# The Jira console appends every organisation change it makes to
# "Jira Scripts\logs\org-changes.json" (written by Jira Scripts\lib\Actions.ps1).
# Each entry holds real ticket keys, reporter names and organisation names.
Jira Scripts/logs/

# --- Draft documentation -----------------------------------------------------
# Hand-written knowledge-base articles waiting to be published to Confluence.
# They quote the REAL organisation name, the real mail domain and real ticket
# numbers, so they must never reach this repository or a shared copy of it.
# They are authored work, not scratch: keep them, just keep them out of git.
/KB-Drafts/

# --- Profile keep lists ------------------------------------------------------
# Remove-UnlistedProfiles takes a -KeepFile listing the people whose Windows
# profile must survive a cleanup, so every one of these files is a list of real
# staff names. One was committed by mistake; these patterns stop that repeating.
# Pass the file by path from anywhere - it never needs to live in the project.
profile_keep.txt
profile-keep.txt
profiles_keep.txt
keep-list.txt
*keep*.txt

# --- Published editions ------------------------------------------------------
# Publish-Standalone.ps1 writes these as sibling folders, but ignore them here
# too in case anyone ever publishes into the project folder by mistake.
/Standalone Editions/
/Desk Side Tool - Core/

# The edition-title file only belongs in a generated edition, never in source.
/toolkit.psd1

# --- Tooling ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code's per-machine permission list. Full of absolute paths from one
# PC, so it is personal to you and not part of the project.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Windows and editor noise ------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
